![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `try-catch` block around `fs.readFileSync` was removed in this refactoring. If the file exists but is not readable (e.g., due to permission issues, locking, or I/O errors), `fs.readFileSync` will throw an unhandled exception and crash the script.

To ensure the system fails closed gracefully, restore the `try-catch` block.

```suggestion
function sha256File(root, relPath) {
  const target = resolvePath(root, relPath);
  if (!target || !fs.existsSync(target)) return null;
  try {
    return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(target)).digest('hex');
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When generating artifact receipts, check if the file exists before attempting to calculate its hash (e.g., SHA-256) to prevent raw file system errors (like ENOENT) from crashing the script when optional files are missing. If the file is missing, record the hash as null and preserve the existence metadata.
</details>

![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `compactSummary` helper function is vulnerable to throwing a `TypeError` if the `summary` parameter is passed as `null` or a non-object value. Since default parameters in JavaScript only apply when the argument is `undefined` (not `null`), passing `null` will bypass the default `{}` and cause a crash when accessing properties like `summary.assertion_count`.

To prevent this, explicitly verify that `summary` is a valid object before dereferencing its properties.

```javascript
  const compactSummary = (summary) => {
    const s = isObject(summary) ? summary : {};
    return {
      assertion_count: Number(s.assertion_count ?? 0),
      question_count: Number(s.question_count ?? 0),
      by_predicate: s.by_predicate ?? {},
      by_risk_tier: s.by_risk_tier ?? {},
      by_topic_component_group: s.by_topic_component_group ?? {},
      by_evidence_family: s.by_evidence_family ?? {},
      external_model_call_count: Number(s.external_model_call_count ?? 0),
    };
  };
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Ensure readback or report generation functions are null-safe and use defensive guards, optional chaining, and safe default objects when dereferencing properties from potentially missing or malformed input artifacts, allowing the script to fail-closed gracefully instead of throwing a TypeError.
</details>

